WEBVTT

00:05.467 --> 00:09.177
<b><i>Tokiyuki's uncle, Yasuie Hojo.</i></b>

00:09.257 --> 00:12.017
<b><i>He is a man who will soon stir up a storm.</i></b>

00:12.097 --> 00:13.097
<b>LET'S DO THIS</b>

00:14.347 --> 00:15.397
<b>Uncle!</b>

00:15.477 --> 00:16.477
<b>GOOD</b>

00:16.557 --> 00:18.357
<b>I'm so relieved you're safe!</b>

00:18.437 --> 00:20.027
<b>Lord Tokiyuki!</b>

00:20.107 --> 00:22.527
<b>I'm the one who's overjoyed
to see you safe!</b>

00:23.357 --> 00:25.357
<b>-Splendid.
-I'm surprised his own uncle</b>

00:25.447 --> 00:26.447
<b>is still alive.</b>

00:26.527 --> 00:27.527
<b>Indeed.</b>

00:27.617 --> 00:30.077
<b>He is the younger brother
of Lord Takatoki himself,</b>

00:30.157 --> 00:32.247
<b>the man at the pinnacle of the shogunate.</b>

00:32.327 --> 00:34.957
<b>He truly was at the very heart of it.</b>

00:35.037 --> 00:36.037
<b>POWER</b>

00:36.957 --> 00:38.837
<b>It was Lord Yasuie who arranged</b>

00:38.917 --> 00:42.087
<b>for Lord Tokiyuki to be entrusted
to my care</b>

00:42.167 --> 00:44.587
<b>during the fall of Kamakura.</b>

00:46.677 --> 00:47.887
<b>Come to think of it,</b>

00:47.967 --> 00:50.927
<b>Uncle, how did you escape that chaos?</b>

00:51.717 --> 00:53.847
<b>I simply passed myself off
as one of Nitta's soldiers.</b>

01:09.777 --> 01:11.907
<b><i>Wounded soldier! Let us through!</i></b>

01:12.447 --> 01:13.747
<b><i>The pain…</i></b>

01:13.827 --> 01:14.827
<b>NO PAIN</b>

01:14.907 --> 01:17.827
<b>I escaped Kamakura by posing
as one of the enemy's wounded soldiers.</b>

01:17.917 --> 01:18.917
<b>NAILED IT</b>

01:18.997 --> 01:20.377
<b>You've got some nerve, boss.</b>

01:20.457 --> 01:22.917
<b>While your clan was dropping like flies,</b>

01:23.007 --> 01:25.587
<b>you still ran away so shamelessly.</b>

01:25.667 --> 01:28.797
<b>Naturally, they asked me to die with them.</b>

01:29.427 --> 01:31.637
<b><i>Come, Lord Yasuie. Join us</i>.</b>

01:32.137 --> 01:34.347
<b>But this is what I told them.</b>

01:34.427 --> 01:35.927
<b>JUST DIDN'T WANT TO DIE</b>

01:36.017 --> 01:37.267
<b>"It's not that I cling to life.</b>

01:37.347 --> 01:39.347
<b>I swear I'll reclaim the throne,</b>

01:39.437 --> 01:42.107
<b>so that your deaths will not be in vain."</b>

01:42.187 --> 01:43.187
<b><i>His forehead…</i></b>

01:43.727 --> 01:45.317
<b><i>I can see something on his forehead.</i></b>

01:46.067 --> 01:47.397
<b>Uncle,</b>

01:47.487 --> 01:50.067
<b>your forehead says
you just didn't want to die.</b>

01:50.157 --> 01:51.277
<b>Oh, my!</b>

01:51.367 --> 01:53.327
<b>Lord Tokiyuki, you're quite observant!</b>

01:55.697 --> 01:58.707
<b>For the past two years, I've traveled
throughout the Tōhoku region,</b>

01:58.787 --> 02:00.877
<b>rallying the remaining Hojo loyalists.</b>

02:01.537 --> 02:03.667
<b>Everywhere we fought,
we lost and had to run.</b>

02:05.257 --> 02:07.257
<b>You are our last hope.</b>

02:08.297 --> 02:09.797
<b>Yorishige Suwa.</b>

02:09.887 --> 02:12.467
<b>Have you made the preparations
to ensure our victory?</b>

02:14.347 --> 02:15.427
<b>Yes.</b>

02:15.517 --> 02:17.557
<b>For the most part,
everything is progressing smoothly.</b>

02:20.267 --> 02:22.477
<b>However,
I have foreseen a troubling future.</b>

02:23.317 --> 02:25.857
<b>I'd like to discuss it
with you over there.</b>

02:25.937 --> 02:27.987
<b>Very well. Let us go!</b>

02:36.697 --> 02:37.787
<b>LET'S DO THIS</b>

02:37.867 --> 02:39.117
<b>Cut it out! Just go already!</b>

02:41.037 --> 02:43.457
<b>He wears everything on his face.</b>

02:44.207 --> 02:45.837
<b>The way he ran for it, you'd never think</b>

02:45.917 --> 02:48.167
<b>he was a prominent figure
of the shogunate.</b>

02:48.667 --> 02:51.837
<b>My uncle has always done
whatever it takes to survive.</b>

02:52.547 --> 02:54.427
<b>He was always scheming
out of self-interest,</b>

02:54.507 --> 02:58.267
<b>obsessed with power and staying alive…</b>

02:58.347 --> 02:59.937
<b>MAKE NICE WITH
THE FIGUREHEAD KID AND CASH IN</b>

03:00.017 --> 03:01.807
<b>…yet it all showed plainly on his face.</b>

03:01.897 --> 03:03.227
<b>ALSO I'M BORED
SO COME PLAY WITH ME</b>

03:03.307 --> 03:05.817
<b>-Come play with me.
-I loved how genuine he was.</b>

03:05.897 --> 03:07.527
<b>He never hid behind the mask of a warrior.</b>

03:32.757 --> 03:37.427
<b>THE ELUSIVE SAMURAI</b>

04:47.577 --> 04:50.127
<b><i>Looks like all the players</i>
<i>are finally coming together.</i></b>

04:51.207 --> 04:53.467
<b><i>So the great battle</i>
<i>is just around the corner.</i></b>

04:54.217 --> 04:56.887
<b><i>That means things are only</i>
<i>going to get more dangerous.</i></b>

04:57.467 --> 04:59.387
<b><i>The brat's never boring to watch.</i></b>

04:59.467 --> 05:01.887
<b>-<i>Don't make me sound like I can't fight!</i>
-<i>But is he really worth</i></b>

05:01.967 --> 05:03.387
<b><i>risking my life for?</i></b>

05:03.477 --> 05:05.057
<b><i>Unlike him,</i></b>

05:05.137 --> 05:08.647
<b><i>I have no enemy to avenge,</i>
<i>nor a clan to protect.</i></b>

05:09.267 --> 05:11.897
<b><i>Getting off here is an option, but…</i></b>

05:13.487 --> 05:16.147
<b><i>I'll think about it later.</i></b>

05:24.997 --> 05:26.077
<b><i>Something's there.</i></b>

05:26.667 --> 05:28.127
<b><i>Or am I imagining it?</i></b>

05:28.207 --> 05:31.627
<b><i>Yorishige has Suwa Grand Shrine</i>
<i>heavily guarded.</i></b>

05:32.127 --> 05:34.047
<b><i>No one should be able</i>
<i>to slip in that easily.</i></b>

05:37.007 --> 05:38.797
<b><i>A thrown weapon?</i></b>

05:46.767 --> 05:48.517
<b>Your instincts are impressive.</b>

05:49.097 --> 05:50.937
<b><i>A tengu mask?</i></b>

05:52.227 --> 05:54.227
<b>So, you're a shinobi after all.</b>

05:54.987 --> 05:58.987
<b>Just as the reports described,
the fox mask of Shinano, Genba Kazama.</b>

05:59.067 --> 06:01.067
<b>Or perhaps his successor.</b>

06:01.697 --> 06:03.657
<b>Either way, it makes no difference.</b>

06:03.737 --> 06:05.157
<b>You'll be dead soon enough.</b>

06:05.867 --> 06:08.917
<b>Wait! Wait! Calm down.</b>

06:08.997 --> 06:10.877
<b>I'm completely unarmed!</b>

06:11.457 --> 06:13.337
<b>Besides, who's this Genba, anyway?</b>

06:13.417 --> 06:17.047
<b>It's just a fox mask for festivals.</b>

06:17.127 --> 06:19.127
<b>Look. Take a closer look.</b>

06:24.807 --> 06:26.887
<b>That was no technique.
Just a parlor trick.</b>

06:28.017 --> 06:30.267
<b>Save your tricks
for the demons in the underworld.</b>

06:35.647 --> 06:37.437
<b>There's a fight over there?</b>

06:38.527 --> 06:40.857
<b>Calling for others to protect you?</b>

06:41.697 --> 06:46.117
<b>At this rate,
you'll never be able to protect your lord.</b>

06:51.377 --> 06:52.827
<b>Genba Kazama.</b>

06:53.377 --> 06:55.547
<b>Not as impressive as the rumors suggest.</b>

06:58.257 --> 07:00.127
<b>-Genba!
-That sound just now…</b>

07:03.217 --> 07:04.967
<b>I need to speak with Yorishige.</b>

07:05.637 --> 07:07.517
<b>This could be a very serious situation.</b>

07:09.427 --> 07:11.057
<b>I've posted guards just as you asked.</b>

07:11.557 --> 07:13.767
<b>No need to worry about an attack
or anyone listening in.</b>

07:14.937 --> 07:18.147
<b>Go on, Genba. Who attacked you?</b>

07:19.817 --> 07:21.317
<b>My old man once told me about them.</b>

07:23.617 --> 07:25.947
<b>A band of shinobi
directly serving Ashikaga.</b>

07:27.077 --> 07:28.077
<b>The Tengu.</b>

07:28.867 --> 07:31.367
<b>With their lightning-fast martial skills
and infiltration techniques,</b>

07:31.457 --> 07:33.457
<b>they say there's no secret
they can't uncover.</b>

07:33.537 --> 07:34.877
<b>KYO - TWO YEARS EARLIER</b>

07:34.957 --> 07:39.167
<b><i>On May 7, 1333, Takauji Ashikaga</i></b>

07:39.257 --> 07:42.377
<b><i>wiped out the shogunate forces in Kyo.</i></b>

07:42.467 --> 07:43.677
<b>THE FOLLOWING DAY, MAY 8,
KŌZUKE PROVINCE</b>

07:43.757 --> 07:46.467
<b><i>The following day, May 8,</i>
<i>in Kōzuke province,</i></b>

07:47.597 --> 07:51.097
<b><i>Takauji's ally, Yoshisada Nitta,</i>
<i>was at a loss.</i></b>

07:52.187 --> 07:55.517
<b><i>The plan was for Lord Takauji</i>
<i>to capture Kyo</i></b>

07:55.607 --> 07:57.397
<b><i>while I launched my attack on Kamakura.</i></b>

07:57.477 --> 07:58.477
<b>YOSHISADA NITTA</b>

07:58.567 --> 08:00.487
<b><i>But I have no idea</i>
<i>what's happening in Kyo.</i></b>

08:01.357 --> 08:04.657
<b><i>Yoshisada Nitta has yet to learn</i>
<i>that Kyo has fallen.</i></b>

08:05.367 --> 08:08.037
<b><i>At the time,</i>
<i>it was impossible for news to travel</i></b>

08:08.117 --> 08:10.617
<b><i>from Kyoto to Gunma in a single day.</i></b>

08:11.207 --> 08:13.667
<b><i>If Lord Takauji has been defeated,</i></b>

08:13.747 --> 08:16.707
<b><i>my small force</i>
<i>cannot hope to defeat the shogunate.</i></b>

08:16.787 --> 08:18.797
<b><i>Should I call off the uprising for now?</i></b>

08:18.877 --> 08:19.917
<b>My lord!</b>

08:23.427 --> 08:25.757
<b>Reinforcements! Around 2,000 strong!</b>

08:25.837 --> 08:28.967
<b>They're our clansmen from Echigo!</b>

08:29.967 --> 08:31.387
<b>How did they know to come?</b>

08:31.477 --> 08:34.387
<b>I hadn't even told my own clan
about the uprising yet.</b>

08:34.477 --> 08:36.727
<b>A Tengu brought us word.</b>

08:37.727 --> 08:38.857
<b>A Tengu?</b>

08:38.937 --> 08:42.737
<b>A single Tengu traveled
throughout Echigo in just one day,</b>

08:43.237 --> 08:47.317
<b>spreading word
that you were rising to attack Kamakura.</b>

08:48.487 --> 08:51.247
<b>How strange indeed.</b>

08:52.827 --> 08:53.827
<b>No matter.</b>

08:53.907 --> 08:55.787
<b>2,000 men will be more than enough.</b>

08:58.037 --> 09:00.547
<b>I hesitate no longer.
We march on Kamakura!</b>

09:00.627 --> 09:02.587
<b>Forward, men!</b>

09:03.087 --> 09:04.087
<b>Aye!</b>

09:05.627 --> 09:08.637
<b><i>Thus, Yoshisada Nitta took advantage</i></b>

09:08.717 --> 09:12.347
<b><i>of the Kamakura shogunate's distraction</i>
<i>with Takauji in Kyo</i></b>

09:12.427 --> 09:15.097
<b><i>and succeeded in bringing down Kamakura.</i></b>

09:16.267 --> 09:17.267
<b>TAIHEIKI, VOLUME TEN</b>

09:17.347 --> 09:21.567
<b><i>This episode of the "Tengu's Message"</i>
<i>is recorded in the Taiheiki,</i></b>

09:21.647 --> 09:23.607
<b><i>a chronicle written by people of the time.</i></b>

09:24.397 --> 09:26.777
<b><i>It is easy enough</i>
<i>to dismiss it as fiction.</i></b>

09:27.317 --> 09:30.527
<b><i>Yet Japan's first simultaneous coup</i>
<i>in the east and west</i></b>

09:31.117 --> 09:34.537
<b><i>was such an extraordinary feat that it</i>
<i>almost defies explanation without a Tengu.</i></b>

09:35.037 --> 09:38.787
<b><i>It suggests that people regarded it</i>
<i>as a mystery even at the time.</i></b>

09:40.417 --> 09:43.007
<b>They are said to travel
about 240 miles in a single day.</b>

09:44.087 --> 09:46.127
<b>Apparently, they played
a major role in the intelligence war</b>

09:46.217 --> 09:47.427
<b>that brought down the shogunate.</b>

09:48.217 --> 09:51.257
<b>I have heard tales of the Tengu as well.</b>

09:52.177 --> 09:54.387
<b>They say there is
a long-established academy</b>

09:54.467 --> 09:56.057
<b>known as the Ashikaga School,</b>

09:56.137 --> 09:59.807
<b>with a division dedicated
to training skilled shinobi.</b>

10:01.147 --> 10:04.437
<b><i>According to historical records,</i>
<i>the first person to employ shinobi</i></b>

10:04.527 --> 10:07.907
<b><i>was Moronao of Ko, the Ashikaga steward.</i></b>

10:09.777 --> 10:13.407
<b>Whatever the case,
we need to call off the great battle.</b>

10:13.487 --> 10:16.367
<b>Otherwise
they'll find evidence of the rebellion,</b>

10:16.457 --> 10:18.287
<b>uncover the brat's true identity,</b>

10:18.367 --> 10:19.667
<b>and that'll be the end of everything.</b>

10:22.587 --> 10:24.207
<b>We must protect Lord Tokiyuki.</b>

10:27.717 --> 10:30.387
<b>Recently, I foresaw an ominous future.</b>

10:30.927 --> 10:35.137
<b>If Lord Tokiyuki stays in Suwa,
he is destined to die.</b>

10:35.807 --> 10:38.227
<b>The wisest course would be
for him to flee as far away as possible.</b>

10:38.847 --> 10:39.977
<b>As Genba said,</b>

10:40.057 --> 10:42.857
<b>our plans require major changes.</b>

10:44.937 --> 10:48.237
<b>Shall we proceed with our plan,
Lord Yasuie?</b>

10:49.487 --> 10:50.487
<b>I'll take care of it.</b>

10:54.787 --> 10:55.987
<b>Lord Tokiyuki.</b>

10:57.577 --> 10:59.497
<b>Leave Shinano</b>

10:59.577 --> 11:02.957
<b>and travel to Kyo with Lord Yasuie.</b>

11:04.247 --> 11:05.247
<b>To Kyo?</b>

11:05.337 --> 11:08.667
<b>The great battle
is scheduled for next month.</b>

11:08.757 --> 11:09.757
<b>LET'S DO THIS</b>

11:09.837 --> 11:14.177
<b>I will be meeting with our allies in Kyo
to plan the uprising.</b>

11:14.257 --> 11:15.257
<b>KYO - SUWA</b>

11:15.347 --> 11:16.637
<b>If you come with me,</b>

11:16.717 --> 11:20.307
<b>we can completely evade
the Tengu's pursuit in the meantime.</b>

11:20.387 --> 11:22.227
<b>The enemy would never suspect</b>

11:22.307 --> 11:25.857
<b>that two members of the Hojo
main family would enter Kyo.</b>

11:25.937 --> 11:27.277
<b>With so many people in Kyo,</b>

11:27.357 --> 11:29.527
<b>it should be easy
to disappear into the crowd.</b>

11:29.607 --> 11:30.607
<b>HOJO</b>

11:30.697 --> 11:33.237
<b>Besides,
if you aspire to become the ruler,</b>

11:33.317 --> 11:36.447
<b>I have always believed
you should see Kyo for yourself.</b>

11:37.997 --> 11:40.577
<b>Kyo is at the forefront
of every aspect of culture.</b>

11:41.327 --> 11:44.537
<b>It is home to extraordinary people,
such as the Emperor,</b>

11:44.627 --> 11:47.047
<b>Takauji, Nitta, Kusunoki, and many others,</b>

11:47.127 --> 11:48.877
<b>though they are our enemies.</b>

11:50.547 --> 11:51.587
<b>Kusunoki?</b>

11:52.717 --> 11:57.347
<b><i>You should've had Kusunoki</i>
<i>teach you the art of war.</i></b>

11:58.057 --> 12:01.637
<b>Naturally, you must avoid
running into any of them.</b>

12:02.347 --> 12:05.307
<b>Even so, there is immeasurable value
in experiencing the atmosphere of Kyo,</b>

12:05.397 --> 12:06.767
<b>where so many brilliant minds gather.</b>

12:11.317 --> 12:13.277
<b>I want to go to Kyo.</b>

12:15.197 --> 12:18.657
<b>Then you should depart
as early as tonight.</b>

12:18.737 --> 12:20.497
<b>-Tonight?
-That soon?</b>

12:20.577 --> 12:24.037
<b>As a matter of fact,
I had anticipated such a situation.</b>

12:24.877 --> 12:29.167
<b>The Suwa Sect has already set our plans
in motion using emergency codes.</b>

12:30.207 --> 12:31.717
<b>What have you been eating these days?</b>

12:32.217 --> 12:33.587
<b>Nozawana pickles.</b>

12:33.677 --> 12:35.507
<b>Nozawana pickles?</b>

12:35.587 --> 12:36.797
<b>That's troublesome.</b>

12:36.887 --> 12:38.757
<b>They really make the rice disappear.</b>

12:38.847 --> 12:40.467
<b>Better watch your waistline.</b>

12:40.557 --> 12:44.097
<b>Indeed. If salted salmon is added as well,
I won't be able to stop eating.</b>

12:44.187 --> 12:45.307
<b>SADAMUNE IS GATHERING TROOPS</b>

12:45.397 --> 12:47.477
<b>IF ICHIKAWA JOINS, THE SITUATION
WILL BECOME DANGEROUS</b>

12:47.557 --> 12:51.107
<b>But how do we get the young lord
out of Shinano?</b>

12:51.187 --> 12:55.697
<b>The Tengu are probably
still watching Suwa Grand Shrine.</b>

12:55.777 --> 12:58.327
<b>If they see a child leaving,
they'll surely become suspicious.</b>

12:58.907 --> 13:02.117
<b>As for that, we shall use the confusion
caused by the mysterious intruder</b>

13:02.197 --> 13:03.457
<b>to our advantage.</b>

13:03.537 --> 13:07.077
<b>We will spirit him away
while covering our tracks.</b>

13:07.827 --> 13:12.167
<b>The only drawback is that
there will be no time for farewells.</b>

13:13.167 --> 13:14.467
<b>A fire!</b>

13:14.547 --> 13:16.967
<b>Lord Yorishige's residence is burning!</b>

13:18.097 --> 13:19.097
<b>Where did it start?</b>

13:19.177 --> 13:20.967
<b>It seems one of the torches fell over!</b>

13:21.677 --> 13:24.807
<b>Damn it! We put out more torches
to guard against intruders,</b>

13:24.887 --> 13:26.847
<b>and now it's come back to bite us.</b>

13:27.477 --> 13:29.897
<b>Dispatch messengers
to the nearby Suwa Sect Warriors.</b>

13:29.977 --> 13:32.397
<b>We'll need more hands
to stop the fire from spreading!</b>

13:32.477 --> 13:33.607
<b>At once!</b>

13:35.277 --> 13:36.277
<b>What's your assessment?</b>

13:37.447 --> 13:40.827
<b>At this point, I can't tell
whether it's simply an accidental fire,</b>

13:40.907 --> 13:44.407
<b>or one staged to destroy documents
proving the rebellion.</b>

13:45.407 --> 13:47.077
<b>Keep your eyes on their movements.</b>

13:47.577 --> 13:48.577
<b>Understood.</b>

13:49.287 --> 13:52.547
<b><i>If this was intentional,</i>
<i>their response was astonishingly swift.</i></b>

13:53.707 --> 13:55.627
<b><i>Had that fox not sensed me…</i></b>

14:01.177 --> 14:02.927
<b>-Are you still with me?
-Yes!</b>

14:03.557 --> 14:05.677
<b>We'll meet up with my retainers
who set out separately.</b>

14:05.767 --> 14:07.057
<b>They're farther ahead.</b>

14:09.017 --> 14:10.897
<b><i>Kyo, too, is full of dangers.</i></b>

14:11.767 --> 14:15.777
<b><i>It always pains me to send you away</i>
<i>based on an uncertain future.</i></b>

14:16.607 --> 14:21.827
<b><i>Yet I believe you will grow even more</i>
<i>through this journey.</i></b>

14:22.987 --> 14:26.457
<b><i>I long to see my child</i>
<i>overcome danger and grow strong.</i></b>

14:27.497 --> 14:28.827
<b><i>As your surrogate father,</i></b>

14:29.327 --> 14:32.247
<b><i>I know that letting you go</i>
<i>is also a form of love.</i></b>

14:32.997 --> 14:34.957
<b><i>Go now!</i></b>

14:35.587 --> 14:38.927
<b>Do not look back, Lord Tokiyuki!</b>

14:42.717 --> 14:46.267
<b><i>Yorishige is following them.</i></b>

14:46.347 --> 14:48.687
<b>Why are you coming too?</b>

14:48.767 --> 14:51.147
<b>Well, I was worried about Lord Tokiyuki.</b>

14:51.227 --> 14:54.527
<b>If the Tengu see you,
our whole cover will be blown.</b>

14:54.607 --> 14:55.937
<b>Hurry back!</b>

14:57.687 --> 14:58.697
<b>Stop making that face.</b>

14:58.777 --> 15:02.567
<b>Father, you're embarrassing yourself.
Go home. Now.</b>

15:03.907 --> 15:06.247
<b>-Go home!
-Go home!</b>

15:06.327 --> 15:08.827
<b>GO HOME GO HOME GO HOME</b>

15:14.247 --> 15:17.587
<b><i>It was in June that Tokiyuki,</i>
<i>filled with anticipation,</i></b>

15:17.667 --> 15:19.507
<b><i>set out for Kyo.</i></b>

15:25.847 --> 15:28.637
<b>That checkpoint belongs to either
the imperial court or the Ashikaga clan.</b>

15:29.347 --> 15:31.727
<b>The inspections look extremely strict.</b>

15:33.147 --> 15:34.147
<b>Besides…</b>

15:34.227 --> 15:35.227
<b>HOJO</b>

15:35.317 --> 15:38.067
<b>Lord Yasuie might as well have
Hojo written across his forehead.</b>

15:38.147 --> 15:39.527
<b>He'll be recognized instantly.</b>

15:42.357 --> 15:43.907
<b>Is there no other way?</b>

15:44.487 --> 15:47.077
<b>The only alternative is to take
the long way over the mountains.</b>

15:47.577 --> 15:49.707
<b>But the slopes are too steep,</b>

15:49.787 --> 15:52.577
<b>and even that would be difficult
unless we leave the horses behind.</b>

15:53.417 --> 15:57.087
<b>No. We're not about to throw away
our horses and baggage</b>

15:57.167 --> 15:58.797
<b>over the likes of them.</b>

15:59.417 --> 16:00.837
<b>I have an idea,</b>

16:00.917 --> 16:03.087
<b>but I'll need about half a day
to get it ready.</b>

16:04.637 --> 16:09.467
<b>There was a post town a little way back.
Pass the time there.</b>

16:10.227 --> 16:13.517
<b>So then, how about
we grab something to eat?</b>

16:13.597 --> 16:16.517
<b>No. I'd rather not waste our money here.</b>

16:17.937 --> 16:20.237
<b>I hear Kyo can get expensive!</b>

16:20.317 --> 16:21.317
<b>ALREADY IN SIGHTSEEING MODE</b>

16:21.397 --> 16:24.697
<b>Exactly! They say Kyo has clothes
and food we've never even seen before!</b>

16:24.777 --> 16:28.037
<b>I want to spend the whole trip
talking like I'm from Kyo.</b>

16:29.037 --> 16:32.117
<b>Father only gave me
a little spending money,</b>

16:32.207 --> 16:33.747
<b>so we need to spend it wisely.</b>

16:37.417 --> 16:38.877
<b>Oops, my apologies.</b>

16:38.957 --> 16:41.417
<b>Must be torture
for you poor folks to look at.</b>

16:41.507 --> 16:42.927
<b>Genba.</b>

16:43.007 --> 16:44.927
<b>Where did you get that much money?</b>

16:46.717 --> 16:48.427
<b>I squeezed it out of Yorishige.</b>

16:49.007 --> 16:51.727
<b>Spotting the enemy shinobi
was no small feat.</b>

16:51.807 --> 16:55.017
<b>I told him Suwa
might've fallen without me.</b>

16:55.727 --> 16:57.147
<b>That's true.</b>

16:57.227 --> 17:00.317
<b>Thanks to you, the enemy never learned
of our plans for the great battle,</b>

17:00.397 --> 17:02.487
<b>and my lord escaped safely.</b>

17:02.567 --> 17:05.197
<b>-That reward is well deserved!
-What?</b>

17:05.277 --> 17:06.907
<b>On that note,</b>

17:07.407 --> 17:09.197
<b>could you lend me some money?</b>

17:09.277 --> 17:11.697
<b>I ran out long ago.</b>

17:12.247 --> 17:15.787
<b>Fubuki kept wasting his money on food
at every post town we passed.</b>

17:15.867 --> 17:19.627
<b>He practically finished off
all the food we brought by himself.</b>

17:24.047 --> 17:26.087
<b>Well, that's your own fault.</b>

17:28.967 --> 17:30.257
<b>I'm stuffed.</b>

17:30.847 --> 17:34.807
<b>There's nothing better than feasting
while the poor look on in envy.</b>

17:36.647 --> 17:38.477
<b>I do feel sorry for Fubuki now.</b>

17:39.017 --> 17:41.607
<b>It may not be much,
but let's bring him something to eat.</b>

17:41.687 --> 17:43.817
<b>Forget that hopeless idiot.</b>

17:43.897 --> 17:45.397
<b>By the way, where's he?</b>

17:45.987 --> 17:47.407
<b>Over in that bamboo grove.</b>

17:47.987 --> 17:50.657
<b>He said he's training
to take his mind off being hungry.</b>

17:58.287 --> 18:01.087
<b>I'm starving.</b>

18:03.627 --> 18:06.507
<b><i>He only missed one meal,</i>
<i>and look at those hungry eyes.</i></b>

18:07.007 --> 18:09.677
<b><i>Looks like he's still got more to him</i>
<i>than meets the eye.</i></b>

18:14.467 --> 18:15.477
<b>Hey.</b>

18:19.517 --> 18:21.317
<b>In return for the food,
answer me something.</b>

18:24.067 --> 18:28.407
<b>That Tengu told me
my fighting style wasn't technique,</b>

18:28.487 --> 18:29.527
<b>just a trick.</b>

18:31.117 --> 18:32.447
<b>I never felt I could beat him.</b>

18:33.157 --> 18:35.407
<b>It felt like there was some
fundamental difference between us.</b>

18:36.207 --> 18:38.577
<b>What do you think it was?</b>

18:40.167 --> 18:43.587
<b>Well, Shinobi techniques
aren't really my expertise.</b>

18:44.337 --> 18:45.707
<b>But if I had to say,</b>

18:45.797 --> 18:49.087
<b>you need to develop techniques
with greater destructive power.</b>

18:49.717 --> 18:52.597
<b>Otherwise,
you don't project any real menace.</b>

18:52.677 --> 18:54.057
<b>Menace?</b>

18:54.637 --> 18:58.227
<b>Your specialty is using tricks
to hold your enemies back.</b>

18:58.807 --> 19:02.147
<b>But on a battlefield
where everyone has accepted death,</b>

19:02.227 --> 19:03.607
<b>tricks won't stop anyone.</b>

19:04.357 --> 19:07.737
<b>If they can feel,
"He could kill me if he wanted to,"</b>

19:07.817 --> 19:09.527
<b>then they'll truly hold back.</b>

19:10.197 --> 19:12.947
<b>If there's a difference between tricks
and true technique, that's it.</b>

19:14.157 --> 19:15.157
<b>I get it.</b>

19:15.657 --> 19:20.117
<b>If I can create truly deadly tools,
simply carrying them concealed</b>

19:20.207 --> 19:21.667
<b>will make my bluff believable.</b>

19:22.167 --> 19:23.167
<b>Precisely so.</b>

19:25.997 --> 19:29.927
<b>By the way, are you sure
Lord Yasuie's plan will work?</b>

19:30.007 --> 19:32.387
<b>If he has "Hojo"
written across his forehead,</b>

19:32.467 --> 19:34.097
<b>there's no way it'll work.</b>

19:34.177 --> 19:35.347
<b>I'm sure it'll work.</b>

19:35.847 --> 19:37.217
<b>Let's go meet up with him.</b>

19:38.017 --> 19:41.187
<b>He told us
to cover ourselves in dirt first.</b>

19:41.267 --> 19:43.307
<b>Genba, the fox mask will draw attention.</b>

19:43.397 --> 19:44.517
<b>Take on a different face.</b>

19:44.607 --> 19:46.147
<b>If we're talking about menace,</b>

19:46.227 --> 19:47.477
<b>my uncle has it as well.</b>

19:47.567 --> 19:50.357
<b>It doesn't matter
that his true feelings show on his face.</b>

19:51.697 --> 19:54.407
<b>He simply forces his way through
with sheer menace.</b>

19:54.907 --> 19:55.907
<b>HOJO
PITIFUL</b>

19:55.987 --> 19:57.407
<b>Have mercy!</b>

19:57.487 --> 20:01.327
<b>If we can't make it to Kyo by tomorrow,
we'll drop dead out here!</b>

20:01.417 --> 20:05.497
<b>I've been promised work as a servant
under Lord Kinmune Saionji!</b>

20:05.587 --> 20:09.127
<b>These poor children lost their mother.</b>

20:09.207 --> 20:11.837
<b>At last,
I'll be able to give them a decent life!</b>

20:11.927 --> 20:14.007
<b>This is the first decent job</b>

20:14.087 --> 20:17.757
<b>a shabby country samurai like me
has ever been offered!</b>

20:17.847 --> 20:21.387
<b>I even borrowed money
to buy this horse and these gifts!</b>

20:21.477 --> 20:23.977
<b>I beg you! Please! Please!</b>

20:26.227 --> 20:27.517
<b>Enough already.</b>

20:27.607 --> 20:28.977
<b>-Get through!
-That hurts!</b>

20:29.067 --> 20:31.447
<b>You're so pitiful
you're making me feel miserable.</b>

20:32.027 --> 20:34.947
<b>Just don't drop dead around here.
It'd be a nuisance.</b>

20:35.027 --> 20:38.487
<b>Yes, sir! Thank you so very much!</b>

20:38.577 --> 20:39.577
<b>WE DID IT</b>

20:41.657 --> 20:43.917
<b>Well, that's about the gist of it.</b>

20:44.917 --> 20:48.457
<b>I skipped meals for half a day,
rolled around in the mountains,</b>

20:48.547 --> 20:50.877
<b>and played the perfect pitiful samurai.</b>

20:52.007 --> 20:54.257
<b>I GOT THIS…</b>

20:55.007 --> 20:58.557
<b>Hiding your true identity behind
a little temporary misery is nothing,</b>

20:58.637 --> 20:59.637
<b>Lord Tokiyuki.</b>

21:00.267 --> 21:03.097
<b>Because we are the mighty Hojo.</b>

21:03.187 --> 21:04.187
<b>HOJO</b>

21:08.567 --> 21:11.817
<b><i>It is said that Yasuie Hojo,</i>
<i>the younger brother of the ruler,</i></b>

21:11.897 --> 21:14.857
<b><i>infiltrated Kyo</i>
<i>by posing as a country samurai</i></b>

21:14.947 --> 21:16.657
<b><i>visiting the capital for the first time.</i></b>

21:16.737 --> 21:17.737
<b>HUH?</b>

21:17.817 --> 21:21.577
<b><i>He survived the bitter power struggles</i>
<i>within the shogunate,</i></b>

21:21.657 --> 21:23.157
<b><i>quietly slipped away when it fell,</i></b>

21:23.247 --> 21:24.247
<b>DOESN'T HURT ONE BIT</b>

21:24.327 --> 21:27.247
<b><i>…incited rebellions wherever he went…</i></b>

21:27.327 --> 21:28.337
<b>LET'S DO THIS</b>

21:28.417 --> 21:31.757
<b><i>…and even infiltrated Kyo</i>
<i>to carry out an unprecedented plan.</i></b>

21:32.377 --> 21:34.507
<b>-Let's do this.
-<i>He was one of the greatest schemers</i></b>

21:34.587 --> 21:35.797
<b><i>of his age.</i></b>

21:36.427 --> 21:38.797
<b><i>Perhaps Tokiyuki inherited his vitality</i></b>

21:38.887 --> 21:41.807
<b><i>not from his frail, spiritless father,</i>
<i>Takatoki,</i></b>

21:41.887 --> 21:44.977
<b><i>but from this uncle instead.</i></b>

21:45.557 --> 21:47.727
<b><i>The brat and the boss get more interesting</i></b>

21:47.807 --> 21:48.977
<b><i>when they're in danger.</i></b>

21:49.607 --> 21:50.727
<b><i>Menace, hey?</i></b>

21:52.727 --> 21:54.947
<b><i>Maybe I'll invent something</i>
<i>truly impressive myself.</i></b>

21:55.607 --> 21:58.317
<b><i>Just so I can see the look</i>
<i>on that Tengu fool's face.</i></b>

21:58.407 --> 22:01.697
<b>Come, Lord Tokiyuki. Kyo is just ahead.</b>

22:01.787 --> 22:04.907
<b>Whenever you need someone's pity,
leave it to me!</b>

23:38.127 --> 23:38.967
<b>EPISODE 20 (YEAR 1335):
IRREPLACEABLE</b>

23:39.047 --> 23:39.877
<b><i>Let's go!</i></b>
